From cew at aris.ss.uci.edu  Wed Aug  5 23:03:58 1998
From: cew at aris.ss.uci.edu (Charles E. (Ted) Wright)
Date: Wed, 05 Aug 1998 16:03:58 -0700
Subject: Re: [S] Alternatives to looping over big dataframes?
In-Reply-To: <9808052133.AA02470@opr.princeton.edu>
References: <9808052133.AA02470@opr.princeton.edu>
Message-ID: <Pine.GSO.3.96.980805155839.18778H-100000@fitts.ss.uci.edu>

Bruce,

Something like the following should do the job for you.

cnts <- table(data1$IDCODE)
whch <- as.numeric(names(cnts[cnts == 11]))
data2 <- data1[match(data1$IDCODE, whch, nomatch=0) > 0, ]

Note that cnts will contain the number of observations associated with each
IDCODE and whch contains the IDCODE of the subjects with 11 observations.

