Please be aware that the 'run it on your server only' solution
is the only one that can REALLY please you.
Anything else is only partially secure; even C can be
decompiled.

So the question boils down to this: how much effort are those
people you are giving the code to willing to spend on finding
out your secrets?

If it is very much, even C won't be sufficient protection.

If it is not so much, it might be sufficient to remove
all comments and scramble all identifiers in your code
(call them a1, a2, a3,.... or give them random names picked
from a dictionary; the latter is extremely confusing)

  Lutz
