Thanks for all who answered my question about the aglorithm used for 
computing confidence limits of median in boxplot() in Splus. Among 
them, Dr. Shawn Boles's comments seem answer my question 
completely. Below are Dr. Shawn's comments: 

Notches are at median +(-) 1.58*((Hinge Spread)/sqrt(n)), where 1.58
arises from combining contribution of;

 1. relationship of hinge spread to population sd
 2. variability of sample median
 3. factor used in setting confidence interval

 see  p. 79 of
@Book{velleman81:abceda,
  author =       {Velleman, Paul F. and Hoaglin, David C.},
  title =        {Applications, Basics, and Computing of Exploratory
  Data Analysis},
  publisher =    {Duxbury Press},
  year =         1981,
  key =          {eda},
}

Appreciated.

