>>>>> "Remigi" == Remigi Lapinskas <Remigi.Lapinskas at maf.vu.lt> writes:

    Remigi> Hello..I am using S-PLUS For Windows Version 3.1 Release 3. What's 
    Remigi> wrong with the following program:

    Remigi> j_4
    Remigi> ff_function(x,j){sin(x*j)}
    Remigi> integrate(ff,lower=0,upper=1,j)

    Remigi> or, in other words, how to pass the value of the parameter j
    Remigi> to the integrate function?  Thank you.

The solution is

        integrate(ff,lower=0,upper=1,j = j)
                                     ====
You need to give the name argument. 
Otherwise, you are accidentally setting subdivisions to 4 (since your j is 4):

 > args(integrate)
 function(f, lower, upper, subdivisions = 100, rel.tol = .Machine$double.eps^
        0.25, abs.tol = rel.tol, keep.xy = F, aux = NULL, ...)

        
